course: dictionary
lesson: 8410
title: Runaway: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, so you must check the words around them to find the right one. «The runaway horse galloped down the hill, and nobody could stop it.» Here runaway describes the horse, and the clue is that nobody could stop it. So runaway means out of control.
explain: Runaway can also be a person. «Two runaways were found safe in the park.» Runaways are people, often children or teenagers, who have left home or another place without permission. Running away is dangerous. If something is wrong at home, tell a trusted adult or call a helpline, such as Childline in the UK or Kids Helpline in Australia.
explain: «The team won by fifty points: it was a runaway win.» A runaway win is one that happens very easily and by a big margin. Try your meaning in the sentence: an easy, big win fits, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Runaway can be a noun (a runaway, runaways) or an adjective (runaway).
fact: «Runaway» as an adjective can mean out of control, as in «a runaway train».
fact: «Runaway» can also mean happening very fast or very easily, as in «a runaway success».
fact: A runaway is a person, often a child or teenager, who has run away from home or from somewhere.
fact: In 2015 a runaway sheep named Chris in Australia was found with a fleece weighing about 40 kilograms.
exercise: «The runaway horse galloped down the hill, and nobody could stop it.» What does runaway mean here? | *Out of control | Very tired and slow | Happy to be ridden
exercise: «The team won by fifty points: it was a runaway win.» What does a runaway win mean? | A late win in the rain | A win that was lost | *An easy, big win
exercise: Maya says a runaway is a shop that sells sweets. What is a runaway, meaning a person? | A shop worker | A type of sweet | *A child or teenager who has run away from home | A kind of bus
test: What should a child do if home feels unsafe and they are thinking of running away? | *Tell a trusted adult or call a helpline | Run off alone at night without telling anyone | Keep it secret and try to manage alone
test: Which sentence uses runaway as an adjective? | *«The runaway train rushed past the station.» | «Two runaways were found in the park.» | «They counted the runaways on the bus.»
exam: What does «runaway success» most likely mean? | A success that happened long ago | *A success that happens very fast or very easily | A success that was lost | A success on a runaway horse
